  "description": "MAFAND-MT (Masakhane Anglo & Franco African News Dataset) — the held-out test split of the African news-translation benchmark: English ↔ 14 African languages (Amharic, Hausa, Igbo, Kinyarwanda, Luganda, Chichewa, Nigerian Pidgin, Shona, Swahili, Setswana, Twi, Xhosa, Yoruba, Zulu) and French ↔ 6 (Bambara, Ghomálá', Éwé, Fon, Mossi, Wolof); both directions scored, matching the paper. Luo is excluded (upstream copyright contradiction). Fetched on demand from the Masakhane repo at a pinned commit; Champollion never hosts the content. Domain: news. Contamination HIGH — public since 2022, in frontier-model crawls — so scores are relative-comparison-only. License CC BY-NC 4.0 (dataset; news source texts carry per-site terms) → non-commercial lanes only; cleared by the license review of 2026-08-24 into the NC research lane: benchmarkable; never in a commercial, prize, or API lane; remote evaluation only over no-train channels.",
